<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Svans</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Svans are a people of Svaneti, a high valley region of north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greater-caucasus">Greater Caucasus</a>, counted as a subgroup of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgians">Georgians</a>. They speak Svan, a Kartvelian language distinct from Georgian. Their villages of medieval defensive towers and churches rich in icons and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuscript">manuscripts</a> are preserved in Upper Svaneti, a World Heritage site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/svans.jpg" alt="Svans" width="320" height="242" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: https://www.facebook.com/photo/?fbid=2558403937526046&amp;amp;set=a.291061063046890 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E1%83%93%E1%83%90%E1%83%93%E1%83%94%E1%83%A8%E1%83%A5%E1%83%94%E1%83%9A%E1%83%98%E1%83%90%E1%83%9C%E1%83%94%E1%83%91%E1%83%98%E1%83%A1_%E1%83%9D%E1%83%AF%E1%83%90%E1%83%AE%E1%83%98.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
